# API route conventions

File-based API routes live in `src/routes/api.*.ts` using `createFileRoute` + `server.handlers`.

## Prefer shared helpers

Use `@src/lib/api-helpers.server.ts`:

- Reads: `setupReadHandler` / `withApiMetrics` / `withDbTiming`
- Mutations: `setupMutationHandler` (auth + CSRF + rate limit wiring)
- Errors: `handleApiError` — never leak stack traces in production

## AuthZ / AuthN

- Authenticate with Clerk-backed helpers in `@src/lib/auth.server.ts` (`requireRole`, `getVerifiedAuth`).
- Authorize with `API_ROLE_SETS` / `AppUserRole` from `@src/lib/roles.ts`.
- Users must only access their own data unless the role is Admin/Manager (or the set defined for that endpoint).

## Mutations must

1. Require CSRF (`requireCSRFToken` / `getCSRFTokenFromRequest` from `@src/lib/csrf.server.ts`).
2. Apply rate limits (`RateLimitPresets` + `requireRateLimit` from `@src/lib/rateLimit.server.ts`).
3. Validate body/query with Zod schemas from `@src/lib/validation.ts` (or colocated schemas that match that style).
4. Use Drizzle — no string-built SQL with user input.
5. Invalidate relevant cache keys via `@src/lib/cache.server.ts` after writes.

## Errors

Throw typed errors from `@src/lib/errors.ts`:

- `ValidationError` (400)
- `UnauthorizedError` / `ForbiddenError` (401/403)
- `NotFoundError` (404)

Return consistent JSON via existing helpers; do not invent ad-hoc error envelopes.

## Client mutations

Browser code should use `fetchWithCsrf` from `@src/lib/csrf.ts` for POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE to CSRF-protected routes.

## Tests

API route changes need Vitest coverage under `src/api/__tests__/`. CI enforces ≥80% statement coverage on API route files via `pnpm run check:api-coverage`.
